A description read from a file or stdin keeps its exact bytes (byte order mark, CRLF, tabs, trailing whitespace); Linear normalizes what it stores and the read-back accepts that, on create and on update.
-- seed.json --
{"Issue": [{"id": "1a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000123", "identifier": "ENG-123", "title": "Described", "description": "Before"}]}
-- file.b64 exact.md --
77u/IA0KQWxwaGEgIA0KCUJldGEKIAk=
-- run --
linear issue create --title Description --team ENG --description-file exact.md --json > create-file.json
-- stderr --
ENG-124 has no --project or --parent. Decide ownership from the candidate Project's full content and the related Initiative content (linear guide issue-authoring), then save the original read and set the project: (if [ -e original.json ] || [ -L original.json ]; then echo 'original.json exists' >&2; exit 1; fi; t=$(mktemp original.json.XXXXXX) || exit; s=0; linear issue view 'ENG-124' --json >| "$t" || { cat "$t" >&2; s=1; }; [ "$s" != 0 ] || ln "$t" original.json || s=1; rm -f "$t"; exit "$s") && linear issue update 'ENG-124' --project <project> --base-file original.json
